summary:
- topic: Athletic Facilities and Field Updates
  text: Athletic Director Todd Livingston presented a progress report on the South
    Portland High School Athletic Complex, noting the project is on time and on budget
    for a May 2027 groundbreaking. Additionally, Director of Operations and Safety
    Mike Nalli confirmed that the South Portland Middle School Field is safe and ready
    for fall soccer and field hockey after successful aeration, overseeding, and fertilization.
- topic: Enrollment and Class Size Adjustments
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina reported a slight year-over-year enrollment
    increase of 20 students, though the long-term trend points downward. To address
    high kindergarten enrollment at Small Elementary School, the administration decided
    to add a new classroom, which will necessitate utilizing a portable building currently
    used for MTSS services.
- topic: Personal Electronic Devices Policy Implementation
  text: 'The board reviewed the implementation plan for Policy JIJC - R: Rules and
    Regulations for Personal Electronic Devices, which enforces a state-mandated bell-to-bell
    ban on personal electronic devices. The rules vary by grade level, with elementary
    devices stored in the main office, middle school devices locked in lockers, and
    high school devices collected in morning lockboxes.'
- topic: Elementary Reconfiguration Workshop Findings
  text: Assistant Superintendent Johanna Prince shared findings from the reconfiguration
    steering committee, highlighting that the community prioritizes socioeconomic
    diversity and stability in school attendance. The district has partnered with
    Sebago Technics for GIS demographic modeling to evaluate potential attendance
    zone and grade-band scenarios ahead of upcoming community forums.
- topic: Public Concerns on Safety and Peer Respect
  text: During public comment, a teacher raised safety and security concerns regarding
    the use of portables at Small Elementary School compared to the main building's
    secure vestibules. Additionally, a middle school student and his mother delivered
    emotional remarks calling for greater peer respect, kindness, and mental health
    support in schools.
- topic: Financial and Policy Approvals
  text: The board approved the consent agenda, the Comprehensive Emergency Management
    Plan, and the first reading of the personal electronic devices rules. The finance
    committee also reported a positive end-of-year fund balance estimate between $71,151
    and $168,508, alongside plans for quarterly financial updates to the City Council.
